{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The festival of unleavened bread.</b> So named on account of the exodus from Egypt to freedom." "<b>Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread.</b> It returned to give warning on its own account. <b>At the season of the month of spring</b> — to teach that the festival of unleavened bread must be fixed in a month that is suitable for offering in it the spring meal-offering of barley, and so that they not appear empty-handed." "<b>And they shall not appear empty-handed.</b> These are the faces of the males who go up on the festival, who appear to me — they and their children are mine."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:02.308640888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}